From bcc27762a8c05d05e8f7dd754ad9043ccae9a3f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:29:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix MLO link metric collection and interface resolution

Link metric responses could miss valid wired or wireless neighbors when interface names, MAC addresses, or MLO parent/child relationships differed between AgentDB, the topology database, and the runtime network state.

- Use targeted NL80211 station requests so responses are tied to the requested station instead of relying on station dumps.

- Resolve interface parent links through sysfs and support MLO/VLAN topology mappings.

- Refresh runtime interface MAC addresses before building link metrics.

- Add topology-discovered fallback interfaces and handle missing MLO backhaul STA interfaces using active BSS information.

- Reject invalid or unknown interfaces and avoid classifying uninitialized VAP configuration data.

- Add diagnostics covering candidate interfaces, neighbor matching, collected metrics, and generated response TLVs.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
